{
  "id": "ep252",
  "duration": 54.421,
  "beats": [
    {
      "start": 0.08,
      "end": 19.22,
      "text": "A dying spacecraft survived its trip to Mercury by sailing on sunlight.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Mariner 10.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mariner_10.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 9.6,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 9.6,
          "end": 19.233,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 19.22,
      "end": 25.42,
      "text": "In November 1973, NASA launched Mariner 10 to attempt the very first interplanetary gravity assist.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Atlas-Centaur launch with Mariner 10.jpg",
        "credit": "Unknown author",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Atlas-Centaur_launch_with_Mariner_10.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 19.233,
          "end": 25.433,
          "kind": "cover",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 25.42,
      "end": 31.42,
      "text": "Soon after takeoff, camera heaters failed and peeling paint tricked the star-tracker into losing its guide star.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Mariner10-IT.jpg",
        "credit": "Mariner10.jpg: NASA / Jet Propulsion Laboratory\nderivative work: Adert (talk)",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mariner10-IT.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 25.433,
          "end": 28.133,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 28.133,
          "end": 31.433,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 31.42,
      "end": 37.28,
      "text": "When attitude control gas ran critically low, engineers gambled on a completely untested maneuver.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Mariner10 - third Mercury encounter - scheme.PNG",
        "credit": "Mariner Venus/Mercury 1973 Project Office, Jet Propulsion Laboratory, NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mariner10_-_third_Mercury_encounter_-_scheme.PNG"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 31.433,
          "end": 37.267,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 37.28,
      "end": 43.38,
      "text": "Controllers angled the solar panels to catch the pressure of solar radiation, using sunlight itself as a rudder.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "ACS3 solar sail fully unfurled.png",
        "credit": "NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:ACS3_solar_sail_fully_unfurled.png"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 37.267,
          "end": 43.367,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 43.38,
      "end": 49.2,
      "text": "That brilliant improvised fix let Venus fling the probe toward Mercury for three historic flybys.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "PIA03101 Mercury's Southern Hemisphere.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA/JPL.",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PIA03101_Mercury%27s_Southern_Hemisphere.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 43.367,
          "end": 46.267,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 46.267,
          "end": 49.2,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 49.2,
      "end": 54.071,
      "text": "Without that sunlight-driven escape, no broken ship could ever sail across the inner solar system.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Mariner 10.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mariner_10.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 49.2,
          "end": 54.433,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
